# roadmap 4.4: a whole scripted game (PLAY=1, 59000 frames) with unlock_players.lua forcing
# hidden players leaves the NVRAM after the audit area (the packed player records and the
# tables after them, records_probe.lua) exactly as the same game with nothing chosen. The
# audits before it differ, as the games differ. Scripts cannot write NVRAM at all
# (nba.write* refuse 0x01400000-0x014FFFFF; luatest). T-unit games only: the Wolf-unit
# headless runs are not repeatable (3.4), so two runs cannot be compared byte for byte there.
script dist/NBAJamRecomp/mods/unlock_players.lua
extra records_probe.lua
game nbajamte nbajamse nbajam
frames 59001
env PLAY=1
run player1=0
run player1=23 player2=55
nbajamte: once records area 66604823
nbajamse: once records area 33952dee
nbajam: once records area 48509b73
